WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:07.959
It was the moment Germans had awaited for
decades.

00:00:07.959 --> 00:00:13.440
And while it was Ronald Reagan who famously
called for the Berlin Wall to be torn down,

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.420
George Bush senior was in office when it finally
happened.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:24.160
Helmut Kohl, the chancellor who oversaw reunification,
once described Bush as a "stroke of luck"

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:29.330
in his country's history -- saying that a
reunited Germany wouldn't have been possible

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:31.949
without his help.

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:37.030
Described as a tireless diplomat, the forty-first
US President helped soften the fronts after

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:41.870
decades of animosity between Washington and
the Eastern bloc.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:47.070
And he vocally supported the idea of German
reunification -- when other European countries

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:50.320
were strongly opposed.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.490
On the 20th anniversary of the fall of Berlin
wall, Bush, Kohl, and former Soviet leader

00:00:55.490 --> 00:01:00.100
Mikhail Gorbachev came together to mark the
occasion.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:09.000
The wall could never erase your dream -- our
dream -- of one Germany: a free Germany, a

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.170
proud Germany, that has thankfully regained
its rightful place among the leading nations

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:18.460
on the Earth.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:23.300
When news of his death broke, Bush's diplomatic
contributions to German unity were at the

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.890
forefront of many people's minds.

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:32.250
On the sidelines of a G20 summit in Argentina,
German chancellor Angela Merkel expressed

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:38.460
her condolences -- as well as an apparent
sentimentality for a different era in transatlantic

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.000
relations.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.390
Helmut Kohl could always rely on this ally
of the Germans in the White House.

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:49.810
During the presidency of George Bush senior,
we experienced the reliability and strength

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:57.600
of the German-American relationship and we
will never forget this experience.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:02.000
George Bush's legacy isn't viewed without
controversy in Germany.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:07.210
Many citizens were deeply opposed to his war
in the Gulf, a war that was co-financed by

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:09.030
their government.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:15.170
Nevertheless, most will remember George Herbert
Walker Bush as a friend and a US president

00:02:15.170 --> 00:05:23.139
who helped show what's possible when countries
work together.

